<title>PORTUGAL: PT unit opens telecom cable to France.</title>
<headline>PT unit opens telecom cable to France.</headline>
<dateline>LISBON 1996-11-06</dateline>
<text>
<p>Marconi, external telecommunications arm of Portugal Telecom, said it inaugurated on Wednesday an optical submarine telecommunications cable between Sesimbra in Portugal and Penmarch in France.</p>
<p>&quot;As a result of an agreement between Marconi and France Telecom, Tagide 2 involved a total investment of 10 billion escudos, which includes a 56 percent participation by Marconi and 29.2 percent by France Telecom,&quot; Marconi said.</p>
<p>The remainder of the investment is shared between 18 other companies involved in the project.</p>
<p>Marconi signed a concession agreement with PT on Wednesday to operate its external telecommunications network until October 20 2000.</p>
<p>-- Lisbon newsroom +351-1-3538254</p>
